# Signal Session — Presage prototype

A consent-first frontend concept for structured interview sessions, optional camera preview, and question or media prompts.

## Run locally

Open `index.html` from a local web server (camera access requires `localhost` or HTTPS). For example, with Python installed:

```powershell
python -m http.server 8000
```

Then visit `http://localhost:8000`.

## Prototype scope

- Before camera access, the participant must review the camera/data disclosure and actively agree; the interviewer must not agree for them. Consent can be withdrawn, which stops the camera and session.
- The camera preview uses the browser's `getUserMedia` API only after agreement and the browser permission prompt. It requests video only, not microphone audio.
- Camera video is only shown as a live preview in the browser. This prototype does not record, analyze, or upload it.
- Pulse and breathing values and waveforms are static sample data. They are not measured by SmartSpectra.
- Facial-expression cues are not connected; expression labels are not a sentiment or truth score.
- Notes, questions, and a selected local image or video exist only in page memory. They are not persisted and are lost when the page is closed or reloaded. Media is not uploaded.
- The app has no account, backend, analytics, SmartSpectra SDK connection, SDK telemetry, or optional AI service. It loads no third-party fonts or AI assets.
- Browser/OS camera-permission settings are controlled by the browser/operating system, not this page. A deployed static host could also have its own access logging policy; this prototype cannot describe a future host's logs or retention.
- The session controls only demonstrate the interface; no SDK session or recording is started.

## SmartSpectra integration

Presage's current SmartSpectra documentation lists Android, iOS, C++, and Node.js/Electron integrations; it does not document a standalone browser SDK. To use live SmartSpectra readings in a web experience, the frontend needs a supported host such as Electron with the Node.js SDK, or a separately implemented trusted service that owns the SDK integration. Do not expose an SDK API key in browser code.

The production integration should replace the sample metrics with SDK-decoded values and their confidence/validation status. Preserve the participant's ability to consent, stop the camera, and understand what is measured and stored. Physiological measurements and facial-expression classifications cannot establish truthfulness and must not be presented as a lie-detection result.

References:

- [SmartSpectra SDK documentation](https://presagetech.com/docs/smartspectra-sdk)
- [Node.js and Electron SDK guide](https://presagetech.com/docs/smartspectra-sdk/nodejs)
- [SmartSpectra model cards and limitations](https://presagetech.com/docs/smartspectra-sdk/model-cards-and-limitations)
